      "writtenOn": "2016-12-20T21:21:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we have any guidance for what keys we\u0027d expect callers to use?  32-bit constants?  ASCIIZ strings?\n\nArbitrary binary blobs are wonderfully generic, but this seems like it\u0027ll lead to a lot of duplicated code where the callers do\n\n#define FOOKEY \"foo\"\nconst char key[] \u003d FOOKEY;\nt \u003d getvar(key, sizeof(key));\n\nwhere if we had a helper function the caller could just do:\n\nt \u003d getvar_s(FOOKEY);\n\nDo we want to maintain a list somewhere of keys in use, to avoid accidental collisions?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 28,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 28,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "f1f71ecf540e9489e4bbee9474aa1b0614960b4e",
